The time period of circular motion of the charged particle is given by
$\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{T}=\frac{2 \pi \mathrm{r}}{\mathrm{v}}=\frac{2 \pi}{\mathrm{v}} \times \frac{\mathrm{mv}}{\mathrm{Bq}} \\
& \mathrm{T}=\frac{2 \pi \mathrm{m}}{\mathrm{Bq}}
\end{aligned}$
Hence, time period of rotation of the charged particle in uniform magnetic field is independent of both $v and R$.
